            <ArticleTitle>Dashboard (in the) knee.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e21-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/003588414X14055925060433</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 19-year-old individual presenting to an orthopaedic outpatient clinic several months following a dashboard knee injury during a road traffic accident with intermittent mechanical symptoms. Despite unremarkable examination findings and normal magnetic resonance imaging, the patient was identified subsequently as having an intra-articular plastic foreign body consistent with a piece of dashboard on arthroscopic knee assessment, the retrieval of which resulted in a complete resolution of symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
